# Regression model for issue #62.  Three shapes in one pool, chosen so
# every assertion the test makes is exact rather than statistical:
#
#   X() <-> Y()   a type change, i.e. a delete + an add on every fire.
#                 Xn + Yn is conserved, so a molecule lost from (or
#                 stranded in) a type index shows up immediately.
#   Z(s) + Z(s)   builds two-molecule complexes alongside free monomers,
#                 so a Species walk over `Z()` sees both the singleton
#                 and the bonded shape.
#   0 -> W()      pure synthesis: the only rule that changes the total
#                 molecule count, which makes the population a molecule
#                 limit stops at exactly predictable.
begin model
begin parameters
  kf   1.0
  kr   1.0
  kon  0.002
  koff 1.0
  ksyn 10.0
  X0   200
  Z0   100
end parameters
begin molecule types
  X()
  Y()
  Z(s)
  W()
end molecule types
begin seed species
  X()  X0
  Y()  0
  Z(s) Z0
  W()  0
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules Xn    X()
  Molecules Yn    Y()
  Molecules Zmol  Z()
  Species   Zsp   Z()
  Species   Zdim  Z(s!1).Z(s!1)
  Species   Zpair Z()==2
  Molecules Wn    W()
end observables
begin reaction rules
  X() -> Y() kf
  Y() -> X() kr
  Z(s) + Z(s) <-> Z(s!1).Z(s!1) kon, koff
  0 -> W() ksyn
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
writeXML()
end actions
